title: The Unemployed
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and c_unemployed_timer <= 0
on-arrival: c_unemployed_timer = 4; month_actions += 1
frequency: 200
is-card: true
tags: movement

= The Unemployed

[? if year = 1919 : Millions of demobilised soldiers have come home to closed munitions works and no jobs. ?][? if year >= 1920 and inflation < 60 : The war industries are gone, and every slump throws thousands more onto the street. ?][? if inflation >= 60 : As the mark collapses, factories close for lack of credit, and the unemployed relief is worth nothing by the time it is paid. ?] Outside the labour exchanges, men queue in their old army coats.

In several towns, our members have formed committees of the unemployed. They want to know what the party will do for them.

- @march: March on the town hall.
- @councils: Build councils of the unemployed.
- @relief: Demand relief together with the unions and the SPD.
- @easy_discard

@march
subtitle: Loud and angry. The police meet it with batons.
on-arrival: militancy += 5; worker_support += 3; repression += 4; offensive_satisfaction += 3; lean_offensive += 1

Thousands of unemployed march behind red flags. The council promises to raise the relief, and the police arrest the speakers.

@councils
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Elected councils of the unemployed, tied to the factory councils. Members join.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids council work.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_councils == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 1.03;
}
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.militancy += 2;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 3;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

The unemployed elect their own councils at the labour exchanges, and send delegates to the works councils of the factories that laid them off.

@relief
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A joint demand for relief and public works. The Right's line.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any deal with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
Q.uspd_relation += 3;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 4;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 3;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The local union cartel and the SPD agree, after long hesitation, to sign a joint appeal with us. The council raises the relief by a third.
